    perf: tighter VRAM footprint estimate + higher budget so models co-run
    
    The old footprint (weights + 0.30*weights + 1.5) overestimated peak VRAM badly
    -- it put Qwen-32B at ~85 GB when measured peak is ~70 GB -- so the scheduler
    ran big models solo and left ~28 GB + most GPU cycles idle (trace collection is
    CPU/IO-bound between short decode bursts, so the GPU sits ~85% idle per model).
    Estimate is now weights*1.10 + 2.0 (Qwen-32B -> ~72 GB, matching reality) and
    the default VRAM budget fraction is 0.80 -> 0.88. Effect: the small-model tail
    packs ~5-wide and a small model can ride alongside the 32B, overlapping idle
    step-gaps. The harness's OOM-microbatch-split remains the safety net.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

